      "content": "Wait, I think there might be some errors in your breakdown. The suffix '-ssa' is the inessive case marker ('in'), not a derivational suffix meaning 'roll'. Also, '-ni' is a first-person singular possessive ('my'), not a moral suffix, and '-ki' is the clitic for 'also/even'. \n\nCould you re-examine it? Specifically, I'm interested in how the morphophonemic changes occur when these morphemes are stacked together. Can you provide a more accurate structural analysis of the segmentation?",
